WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:06.590
In A Song of Ice and Fire and Game of Thrones,
Westeros is threatened by an army of the dead

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:12.040
bringing a night that never ends. According
to prophecy, the only hope is a hero, known

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.350
as Azor Ahai, or the prince that was promised. The text suggests that Jon or Daenerys or

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.519
both are Azor Ahai. But could the saviour
be someone… furrier?

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:27.980
Ser Pounce is one of King Tommen's kittens,
along with Lady Whiskers and Boots. The kittens

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.360
are given to him by Margaery Tyrell, and
we're not told where Margaery gets the kittens,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.590
but we can actually make a pretty good guess.
Margaery lives in the Red Keep, and the Keep

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.970
is “full of cats”, including “kittens”. We also know Margaery likes to look after

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.100
the poor and vulnerable. So maybe Margaery
finds Ser Pounce and the others as strays

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.870
in the Keep, and offers them to Tommen as
a way of caring for them. If the kittens are

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:57.370
strays from the Keep, we can work out who
their father may be. Arya chases many cats

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:02.620
around the Keep, but one of them is special
– a tomcat with black fur, one ear and a

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.859
reputation. He snatches food out of Tywin’s
fingers, scratches Joffrey, attacks ravens

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:12.229
in the rookery. A gold cloak calls him a
“black bastard”, “Older than sin and

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.869
twice as mean”. Tommen calls him “The
bad cat”, but we might call him “the

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:21.810
bad pussy”. Anyway, so this is a black cat
living in the Red Keep. It just so happens

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:25.850
that Ser Pounce and his siblings are also
black cats, who may have been born in the

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:30.539
Red Keep. We’ve been told, of course, that
“the seed is strong” – black hair colour

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:37.079
can indicate parentage. So it’s very possible,
likely, even, that this tomcat is Ser Pounce’s

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:41.140
father. The reason why that would be cool
is that the tomcat is described as “the

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:47.389
real king of the castle”. If Ser Pounce’s
father is a king, Ser Pounce is a prince.

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:51.780
And Tommen makes a “promise” to Cersei
to let him have kittens, making Ser Pounce

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:58.229
a prince that was promised – a phrase used
to refer to Azor Ahai. Is it possible that

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:02.299
Ser Pounce is the prophesied saviour of the
world?

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:09.580
Let’s do this properly, see if Ser Pounce
fits what he know of the hero Azor Ahai. For starters, it’s

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.600
said that “The dragon must have three heads”, and Ser Pounce has Lady Whiskers and Boots.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:20.170
But the most important stuff are these seven
signs. Azor Ahai is prophesied to be born

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.950
beneath a bleeding star, apparently referring
to the “red comet” that appears at the

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.470
end of the first book. We don’t know when
Ser Pounce is born, but we do know he’s

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:32.390
still a kitten in Dance, which is roughly
a year after the last sighting of the comet

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:37.890
in Clash. It apparently takes about a year
until a kitten is called a cat, so it's totally possible

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:43.380
that Ser Pounce is literally born beneath
the comet – the bleeding star. Azor Ahai

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:48.330
is prophesied to be born amidst salt and smoke. The Red Keep overlooks the salty sea, or

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:53.230
at least Blackwater Bay which Davos says is
salty, and the Keep is lit by torches that

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:59.880
produce smoke. So that all pretty much fits.
Azor Ahai is prophesied to have a “red”

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.730
or “burning sword”, which Sam and Jon
suggest might just mean a Valyrian steel sword.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.800
As far as we know, Ser Pounce does not have
a sword, in fact he doesn’t have thumbs,

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:15.700
which may pose a problem with the grip.
But we do know that Littlefinger has a Valyrian

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.650
steel knife, which might be small enough
for a cat to hold, like, ah with his mouth?

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:27.750
Ah, so yeah put that down as a maybe. Azor
Ahai is said to need a sacrifice, and Ser

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:33.230
Pounce… catches a mouse, for what that’s
worth. Azor Ahai has something to do with

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.610
dragons, or to “wake dragons out of stone”. Dany’s dragon eggs are described as stone,

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:44.140
and she wakes them by making them hatch.
Could the dragon skulls in the Red Keep be

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:50.650
called stone dragons? Could Ser Pounce, in some sense, wake them, bring them back to life? Will we

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:55.210
see Ser Pounce riding a reanimated skeletal
dragon, what could be called “a flaming

00:03:55.210 --> 00:04:01.280
sword above the world”? Eeh, probably not.
Azor Ahai is prophesied to be born of the

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:07.470
line of The Mad King Aerys and Rhaella Targaryen. This one is tricky, but Rhaella had many

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:13.070
miscarriages and stillbirths, and when Daenerys
suffers a stillbirth, albeit a magic-induced

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:18.590
one, the child resembles a lizard or dragon. If Targaryens can give birth to dragon-like

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:24.849
children, why not cat-like children? Could
Queen Rhaella Targaryen have given birth to

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:30.449
the black tomcat that fathered Ser Pounce?
Interestingly, we do know that there was a

00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:36.199
black kitten in the Targaryen family at the
time, a pet of Princess Rhaenys, called Balerion.

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:40.840
Varys tells us about this kitten, and wonders
what happened to it. Many fans believe that

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.949
Balerion stayed in the Red Keep and grew up
to be this tomcat – they’re both black,

00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:51.539
the tomcat is old, and he seems to hate Lannisters,
the family that killed his Targaryen masters.

00:04:51.539 --> 00:04:56.879
George R. R. Martin has said that this theory
“Could be” true – the tomcat, Ser Pounce’s

00:04:56.879 --> 00:05:02.740
possible father, could be Balerion, the Targaryen
pet. So if you’re willing to believe that

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:07.610
Queen Rhaella somehow gave birth to Balerion
the cat, which, you shouldn’t, but if you

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:12.860
are, that means Ser Pounce, son of Balerion,
is a secret Targaryen, of the line of Aerys

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:19.189
and Rhaella – he's the rightful ruler of Westeros,
ahead of Daenerys. For now, he bides his time

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:23.289
at Tommen’s side, but soon will rise to
“defend his rights” and fight for the

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:30.139
light as Azor Ahai, the Pounce that was promised,
King Pounce Targaryen the First, “a hero

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:38.259
to deliver the world from darkness”.
Except, not really, right?

00:05:38.259 --> 00:05:43.710
Syrio Forel tells Arya a story. He says the
Sealord of Braavos kept exotic creatures from

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:48.979
around the world, and one day he showed people
one of his animals. People saw “a fabulous”,

00:05:48.979 --> 00:05:55.599
exotic “beast”, but Syrio looked and said
it’s a cat. Just “an ordinary cat, no

00:05:55.599 --> 00:05:59.969
more”. People saw “a fabulous beast”
because that’s what they expected and wanted

00:05:59.969 --> 00:06:05.399
to see. Syrio says “The heart lies and the
head plays tricks … Look with your eyes

00:06:05.399 --> 00:06:10.249
… Then comes the thinking … and in that
way knowing the truth”. The truth is that

00:06:10.249 --> 00:06:16.120
Ser Pounce is a cat. Yes, he can maybe kinda
fit the signs of Azor Ahai, but anything can

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.090
seem to fit such vague criteria when there’s
so much material to cram into them. This is

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:26.219
how people believe in quack medicine and young-Earth
creationism and Illuminati conspiracism, and

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:30.659
maybe all the little lies we tell ourselves
each day – pick specific details, apply

00:06:30.659 --> 00:06:35.819
some wishful thinking, and you can believe
whatever you want to believe. To find the truth,

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:40.529
you’ve gotta step back, look at the whole
body of evidence, the broader context, the

00:06:40.529 --> 00:06:46.759
bigger picture, in this case, that A Song
of Ice and Fire is a story of human struggle,

00:06:46.759 --> 00:06:52.779
centred on people like Jon and Daenerys. The
truth is that Ser Pounce is “an ordinary

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:59.729
cat, no more”. But he could still be the
kitten of Balerion, so that’s pretty cool anyway.

